From 0fa345d907215d12692ac78e69383f830a4c8001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yijie Zhu <yz994@cornell.edu>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:31:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Simulation-tabulated IA (sim_IA.c) on the halo-IA reduction
 path

Port of sim_IA from halo_ia_debug onto main. sim_IA.c/h are copied
unchanged from the branch tip (da9152b). IA_code = 3 (IA_CODE_SIM) routes
the Limber ss and gs engines through the existing include_halo_IA
reduction with f_rc = 0, KHI[0] = 0, KHI[1] = -P_sim_dE, KHI[2] = P_sim_EE,
so no new integrand code is needed. Paths without halo-IA support (ks,
non-Limber gs, scale-cut responses) refuse IA_code = 3. C FAST-PT bias
now runs for any IA_code other than 1 (Python FAST-PT), so nonlinear
galaxy bias keeps working with IA_code = 3. Interface: init_IA_sim,
set_IA_sim_shape_convention, set_IA_sim_erms, set_IA_sim_erms_hinfo,
set_IA_sim_window; each redraws nuisance.random_ia.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0135VCYFFeAoL9ZXf4QAGX4J
